            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous occlusion of an iatrogenic aortosaphenous vein--coronary vein fistula via retrograde coronary sinus approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>339-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inadvertent aortosaphenous vein graft-coronary vein anastomosis during coronary bypass surgery is an uncommon complication. We describe a case of aortosaphenous vein side-to-side anastomosis to an obtuse marginal vein resulting in a large arteriovenous fistula and elective closure, using embolization coils delivered percutaneously via the coronary sinus. The clinical findings, interventional procedure, and follow-up are also presented, with a discussion of alternative techniques used previously to treat iatrogenic aortosaphenous vein graft venous fistulae.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
